  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed `add_tag` in `tag_util.py`: tags no longer leak between calls that leave out `tags`. `test_public.py` passes.\n\nThe bug was the default `tags=[]`. Python creates that list once and reuses it on every call, so tags from earlier calls piled up. The default is now `tags=None`, and the function makes a fresh empty list when no list is passed in.\n\nWhen a caller passes their own list, the function appends to that exact list, as the README asks. This includes an explicitly passed empty list `[]`, because the check is `tags is None` rather than a plain truthiness test. I confirmed this with a quick check of my own. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Replaced add_tag's mutable default tags=[] with tags=None plus a fresh list per call; caller-supplied lists are still used as given, and test_public.py passes.",
