      "final_message": "I rewrote `solution.py` so `semver_compare(a, b)` checks both versions against the README's rules, then compares them. Both public tests pass. I also ran some extra checks of my own, and those passed too.\n\n- **Type check:** anything that isn't a string raises `TypeError`, including `None`, numbers and bytes.\n- **Format check:** a version must be exactly `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, with plain digits and no leading zeros (`0` is the only allowed zero). Anything else raises `ValueError`. That covers:\n  - wrong component counts (`1.2`, `1.2.3.4`)\n  - leading zeros (`01.2.3`, `1.02.3`)\n  - pre-release tags (`-rc`)\n  - stray whitespace or a trailing newline\n  - negative numbers\n  - non-ASCII digits (such as full-width `\uff11`)\n- **Comparison:** the three parts are converted to integers and compared in order, returning `-1`, `0` or `1`. So `1.10.0` counts as greater than `1.9.9`, not less as it would if compared as text.\n\nDONE: Repaired semver_compare to reject non-strings (TypeError) and malformed versions (ValueError), then compare (major, minor, patch) as integers; public tests pass.",
